## Nikki, OpenClash and AdGuard Home are installed only on request, but every
## dependency each of them declares is already in the image, so `apk add`
## resolves offline against the image's own packages and does not pull a tree.
##
## Checked against each Makefile:
##   nikki            +ca-bundle +curl +yq firewall4 +ip-full +kmod-inet-diag
##                    +kmod-nft-socket +kmod-nft-tproxy +kmod-tun +kmod-dummy
##                    +mihomo
##   mihomo-meta      +ca-bundle +ip-full +kmod-inet-diag +kmod-tun
##   luci-app-nikki   +luci-base +nikki
##   luci-app-openclash +dnsmasq-full +bash +curl +ca-bundle +ip-full +ruby
##                    +ruby-yaml +kmod-tun +unzip
##   adguardhome      +ca-bundle          (static Go binary, nothing else)
##   luci-app-adguardhome +ca-certs +curl (ca-certs is PROVIDED by
##                    ca-certificates, already selected)
##
## The kmods and firewall4/dnsmasq-full are selected above; these are the
## userland ones plus the two kmods that were missing.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_yq=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_bash=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_ruby=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_ruby-yaml=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-dummy=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_firewall4=y

## AdGuard Home: NOT installed, available from the feeds.
##
## It is a ~30 MB Go binary plus a web root; baking it into the image costs
## more space than most of the rest of the added packages combined, and the
## people who want it are a minority. It is built as a package and published
## next to the image, so `apk add adguardhome luci-app-adguardhome` installs it
## on demand. luci-app-custom (below) is the one-click installer for the
## AdGuard + PassWall2 DNS chain.
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_adguardhome is not set
# CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci-app-adguardhome is not set
## Dependencies those two need are already in the image so the on-demand
## install does not pull a tree: ca-bundle, curl, and the nft/conntrack set
## listed under QUIC above. AdGuard Home itself is a static Go binary and
## needs nothing else at runtime.

## BYTE runtime: TTL/HopLimit rewrite, MTU clamp, IPv6 sanity, self-check.
# The nftables source package builds nftables-json (and nftables-nojson);
# there is no bare `nftables` binary package on this tree.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_nftables-json=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-nft-core=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-nft-nat=y

## RAM swap via zram: 433 MB of compressed swap on a 1 GB box.
##
## zram-swap is the script; kmod-zram is what it needs, and the compressor is a
## separate module. lzo-rle is chosen in byte/files/etc/config/system because it
## is the fastest and the only one this kernel ships: CONFIG_CRYPTO_LZ4 is off
## and there is no *lz4* module in /lib/modules, so configuring 'lz4' makes
## zram-swap log "compression algorithm 'lz4' is not supported", exit 0 anyway,
## and leave a 433 MB device with 0 kB of swap. Pinning the backend here means
## the symbol cannot be silently dropped by a rebase.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_zram-swap=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-zram=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-lib-lzo=y
CONFIG_KERNEL_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZO=y
CONFIG_KERNEL_ZRAM_DEF_COMP_LZORLE=y
# lz4/lz4hc/zstd backends stay off: no module and no userspace consumer.
# CONFIG_KERNEL_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4 is not set
# CONFIG_KERNEL_ZRAM_BACKEND_LZ4HC is not set
# CONFIG_KERNEL_ZRAM_BACKEND_ZSTD is not set
# Writeback is forced off by the kernel package's own KCONFIG
# (CONFIG_ZRAM_WRITEBACK=n): it would need a backing block device, and there is
# none on this board. Not a Kconfig symbol here, so it is not set from this
# file.

## One page for the image-specific switches that have no home of their own: the
## NSS/ECM offload toggle and the AdGuard Home + PassWall2 DNS setup
## (Ace1337z's installer, vendored). Both AdGuard packages are installed on
## demand, not baked in. TTL is deliberately NOT on this page - it belongs to
## QModem's own package, below; the page only reports its state.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci-app-custom=y

## TTL / HopLimit rewrite: QModem's own implementation, and the only one.
##
## This replaced the in-tree byte-ttl service. Shipping both meant two nft
## rulesets rewriting the same packets, and whichever loaded last won - the
## qmodem_ttl LuCI page and Services -> Custom would then disagree about what
## was actually running. The same reasoning excludes dotycat's
## luci-app-nft-ttl (see feeds.exclude), which also keys on iifname br-lan and
## so rewrites LAN-to-LAN traffic besides.
##
## The fw4 variant is the one for this image (firewall4 is what the tree
## ships): js UI, /etc/config/qmodem_ttl, and an init script that writes
## /etc/nftables.d/99-reset-ttl-from-br-lan.nft and disables the hardware fast
## paths that would otherwise let packets past netfilter with their original
## TTL. luci-app-qmodem-ttl is the iptables flavour, CONFLICTS with it, and
## depends on the excluded legacy UI.
CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci-app-qmodem-ttlfw4=y

## RJ11 phone port: SLIC kernel module, the daemon and its LuCI page.
## fxsd 0.5.0 drives the AT modem through the 'at-daemon' ubus object, which
## ubus-at-daemon provides (from the qmodem feed, above). Without it the phone
## sits at "Waiting for the modem".
CONFIG_PACKAGE_kmod-aw1000-fxs=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_fxsd=y
CONFIG_PACKAGE_luci-app-fxs=y

## USB storage: mass storage + UAS, common filesystems, automount under
